<section class="section" aria-labelledby="relocation-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Voluntary Relocation</p>
    <h2 id="relocation-heading">Published status and safeguards must be read together</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Relocation is governed by rights recognition, voluntary choice, compensation and rehabilitation
      requirements. A village-status statement does not establish the outcome for every household.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="resource-guidance-grid">
    <div><strong>Laxmipura</strong><span>Reported completely relocated in the September 2022 MEE.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Kherli Bawadi and Ghati</strong><span>Reported relocated except for absentee landholders in the September 2022 MEE.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Mashalpura</strong><span>Reported partially relocated in the September 2022 MEE.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Damodarpura and Giridharpura</strong><span>Relocation deliberations were reported underway in the September 2022 MEE.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="source-note">
    NTCA’s document register records that central funding assistance for voluntary village relocation was
    enhanced from ₹10 lakh to ₹15 lakh per eligible family on 8 April 2021. Rajasthan’s 24 July 2025 order
    replaces the State’s 2022 land-package provisions and retains the choice between the prescribed land
    package and the ₹15 lakh cash option, or the NTCA amount applicable at the time. Eligibility, voluntary
    option selection, rights settlement and actual payment must be verified from the applicable household and
    government record; a published package does not prove an MHTR payment or rehabilitation outcome.
    See the <a href="/resources/documents/rajasthan-voluntary-village-relocation-package-2025/">locally archived Rajasthan order and original-source record</a>.
  </p>
</section>

