<section class="section" aria-labelledby="audit-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Historical Audit Context</p>
    <h2 id="audit-heading">How the 2025 CAG report is used on this page</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Scope</h3>
      <p>
        Rajasthan Report No. 5 of 2025 contains a Subject Specific Compliance Audit of tiger-reserve
        management for FY2016–17 to FY2020–21, with later position updates identified in the report.
        It was tabled on 19 February 2026.
        Its executive summary discusses staffing, protection, invasive species, land security,
        village relocation and community participation across the State system.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Limits</h3>
      <p>
        State-wide findings are not attributed to MHTR alone. The reported relocation aggregate—108
        planned villages across Ranthambore, Sariska and MHTR, with 15 fully and 17 partially relocated
        by March 2023—is a combined historical figure, not the current MHTR count.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="source-note">
    <a href="/resources/documents/cag-rajasthan-forest-management-2025/">Open the locally archived CAG chapter and original-source record</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="public-help" aria-labelledby="public-help-heading">
  <div class="source-panel">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Official Public Help</p>
      <h2 id="public-help-heading">Wildlife rescue, forest fire and encroachment: 1926</h2>
      <p>
        Rajasthan Forest Department lists the toll-free helpline <strong>1926</strong> for animal rescue,
        forest fire and encroachment reports. Reports should describe the event and a safe, general
        location; members of the public should not chase, crowd, feed or handle wildlife.
      </p>
      <p>
        The April 2026 State order sets ex-gratia amounts for wildlife-caused human death or permanent
        incapacitation at <strong>₹10 lakh</strong>, grievous injury at <strong>₹2 lakh</strong>, and minor
        injury at <strong>₹25,000</strong>, subject to certification, procedure and the other conditions in the order.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="source-actions">
      <a class="button-link" href="tel:1926">Call 1926</a>
      <a class="button-link" href="/resources/documents/rajasthan-wildlife-ex-gratia-order-2026/">Open archived compensation order</a>
      <a class="button-link button-link-secondary" href="https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/raj/forest/en/home.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Forest Department portal</a>
    </div>
